      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Northstar Credit Analytics has raised Coppermere Components' senior unsecured bond rating to BBB from BBB-, with a stable outlook. The Amberford manufacturer supplies replacement parts for industrial pumps and ventilation equipment. The upgrade reflects sustained debt reduction, a broader customer base and improved cash collection."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Debt fell to KRN 126 million at the end of August from KRN 171 million eighteen months earlier. Over the same period, debt relative to annual operating profit before depreciation declined from 3.8 times to 2.6 times. The largest customer now accounts for 14% of revenue, compared with 23% two years ago. Replacement orders provide more consistent demand than sales tied to new construction."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Cash and committed facilities comfortably cover the company's lowest projected three-month funding position under Northstar's revised methodology. The stable outlook assumes moderate investment and no large debt-funded acquisition. A downgrade could follow if debt rises above 3.5 times operating profit for a sustained period or customer concentration increases materially."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-10-20",
      "title": "Kestrian Retail Bond Issuers Enter Winter with Uneven Cash Buffers",
      "authors": ["Elise Dorne", "Nalin Verdan"],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Northstar Credit Analytics has maintained a negative outlook for Kestrian discretionary retailers in its latest sector review. Households are limiting larger purchases, while retailers have already paid for much of their winter stock. The agency expects differences in cash reserves to matter more than modest changes in reported sales."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Among six rated issuers, stock values at the end of September were 9% higher than a year earlier, while sales for the preceding three months rose only 1%. Two chains operating mainly in Saltmarsh and Kestrel Bay increased promotional discounts to clear older goods. Across the sample, average operating margins before depreciation fell to 6.2% from 7.1%."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Four issuers have committed facilities extending beyond their seasonal borrowing peak. The remaining two rely more heavily on cash generated during winter trading. Northstar is testing slower stock sales and delayed supplier credit separately for each company. The sector outlook does not imply that every retailer will be downgraded, and no individual rating changes accompany this report."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-10-22",
      "title": "Val-Brume Packaging Rating Affirmed After Investment Spending Is Reduced",
      "authors": ["Céline Maret", "Dario Selven"],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Northstar Credit Analytics has affirmed Val-Brume Packaging's BB+ senior unsecured bond rating and stable outlook after the company reduced its investment budget. Management has deferred a second printing line, cutting planned spending for the current financial year to KRN 18 million from KRN 34 million."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "The decision preserves cash while the company addresses the working capital pressures behind its September downgrade. Unrestricted cash stood at KRN 22 million at the end of September, with KRN 35 million still available under its committed facility. Early collections from overdue customers helped the improvement, although one month of stronger receipts does not establish a sustained recovery."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Northstar continues to expect debt near 5.0 times annual operating profit before depreciation in the near term. The revised liquidity assessment supports the existing rating because available resources cover projected seasonal needs. An upgrade would require durable earnings recovery and lower debt. Renewed cash outflows, weaker facility access or substantial additional borrowing could lead to another downgrade."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "releases": [
    {
      "date": "2026-08-17",
      "title": "GreenBasket opens new neighbourhood store in eastern Amberford",
      "author": "Mara Fenwick",
      "blocks": [
        {
